  "units": "cm",
  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for the power of a lens, book pages 264–266, topic 9.4.3, next to চিত্র ৯.২৭ and the closing নিজে করো. On an optical bench, a ray box's five parallel beams are traced exactly through glass lenses: the book's glasses lens (f = 40 cm, +2.5 ডায়াপটার), then more curved ones (20 cm, 10 cm) and two concave lenses. The student sees a pencil at the same distance look bigger through the lens with the shorter focal length (চিত্র ৯.২৭), measures each lens's f on the scale, and reads P = 1/f in dioptres, positive for convex and negative for concave, on a live P–f graph. A five-question test reads powers off the scale and does the book's নিজে করো.",
